    "Dental sealants — also called fissure sealants — are thin protective coatings painted onto the chewing surfaces of back teeth to stop food and bacteria from settling in deep pits and fissures. In Australia, <a href=\"/blog/tooth-decay/\">tooth decay</a> remains the most common chronic disease among children: around one-third of children have decay in their baby teeth by age five, and decay in permanent teeth rises sharply in the early teenage years — exactly when the first and second permanent molars erupt.",
